{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["כל ימי השמה תשבות — all the seventy years of the Babylonian exile. Our Rabbis explained: corresponding to the years it should have observed [sabbatical years] but did not observe." "תשבות — with a munach before an etnaḥta; but without an etnaḥta, then אז תשבת הארץ has a pataḥ. And likewise וימת and וינס with an etnaḥta — all of them have a munach. וַיָמֹת, הים ראה וינס."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "Rashbam's examples illustrate a cantillation rule: when the same word form (e.g. תשבות, וימת, וינס) appears with or without an etnaḥta, the preceding munach and vowel quality shift accordingly. The last line quotes forms where these words carry different vocalization or accentuation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:32.132705095Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}